    "title": "Dutchmen down Royalton Royals - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Bowman ,\n2 days ago\nThe Royalton Royals were defeated 43-22 at home by the Melrose Dutchmen in football action on Friday, Sept. 26.\nMelrose jumped out to a 15-0 lead on a five-yard touchdown run in the first quarter by Becken Elfering and then Elfering threw a 17-yard TD pass to Teague Dusha in the second quarter.\nRoyalton answered with a one-yard touchdown by Kirk Yourczek (two-point conversion was successful) to cut the deficit to 15-8.\nMelrose then ripped off a 75-yard kickoff return for a touchdown to lead 22-8 at halftime.\nAfter a 10-yard TD run by Melrose, Yourczek scored his second major on a 29-yard run.\nLeading 29-14, Melrose scored a pair of touchdowns before Royalton quarterback Connor Boser closed out the game’s scoring with a 55-yard touchdown in the fourth quarter.\nYourczek was 4-of-9 passing for 63 yards and he also carried the ball 16 times for 80 yards. Boser ran nine times for 77 yards.\nRoyalton receptions were made by Chaz Psyck (two, 30 yards), Max Vannurden (catch, 18 yards), Jordan Hawkins (catch, 15 yards), and Yourczek (catch, 10 yards).\nThe Royals’ defensive leaders were Kane Neisen (eight tackles), Colton Burggraff (six tackles), Yourczek (four tackles, assisted tackle, tackle for loss), and Hawkins (four tackles, assisted tackle).\nRoyalton (3-2) played at Osakis on Friday, Oct. 3, but no score was available at press time. The Royals will host Paynesville on Friday, Oct. 10. Kickoff is 7 p.m.",
